<p>Iran said vessels it classifies as &quot;non-hostile&quot; can transit the Strait of Hormuz if they coordinate with Iranian authorities and meet Iranian safety and security requirements. Tehran said ships linked to the United States, Israel, and other countries it accuses of taking part in attacks on Iran would not qualify. Caixin, as cited by Semafor, said one Chinese-owned cargo ship has already passed through under the new arrangement, an early sign that at least some commercial traffic may resume. The move matters because the U.S.-Israeli war against Iran has all but halted traffic through one of the world’s most important energy chokepoints, disrupting shipments of about one-fifth of global oil and liquefied natural gas, according to Reuters reporting cited by Al-Monitor. President Trump said talks are underway to end the war, and Iran’s announcement offered the possibility of limited relief for global shipping and energy markets, even though it remains unclear how many shipowners will risk the route.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/zUBI0PjzngTfyLN9MuUL6XLGmPSWTdMOsoR182g4VbGc6RTuvlBJfI4njuUki_MtaLbl-wsiYiUZiMdDyfmKC2PMmRHOoSOuiX3y8eU4VnFT--Jnl9HD_u5_UIH0AT2YaitoEYmP4yHaFOpR1S2H_iPgS8hu59CWEi8f8Kzy_eEoeeo_Ts21iuJZc_u7XX8A09TcW16vF_Xlj15kyXvaYQ' alt='Cargo ships in the Gulf, near the Strait of Hormuz, seen from the United Arab Emirates earlier this month.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Formal notice: Reuters, citing the Financial Times, said Iran laid out the transit terms in a letter to member states of the International Maritime Organization and to the United Nations.</li><li>Safety wording: Al Jazeera said Tehran told qualifying ships they could pass safely through the strait.</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/03/24/2026/iran-allows-china-ship-to-transit-strait-of-hormuz'>Iran allows China ship to transit Strait of Hormuz</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/iran-says-non-hostile-ships-can-transit-strait-hormuz-ft-reports'>Iran says &#x27;non-hostile&#x27; ships can transit Strait of Hormuz, FT reports</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/24/world/middleeast/iran-strait-of-hormuz-ships.html'>Iran Says ‘Non-Hostile’ Ships Can Sail Through the Strait of Hormuz</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/iran-says-non-hostile-ships-can-transit-strait-of-hormuz-ft-reports'>Iran tells UN: ‘Non-hostile’ ships can transit Strait of Hormuz</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2026/3/25/iran-says-non-hostile-ships-can-pass-safely-through-strait-of-hormuz'>Iran says ‘non-hostile’ ships can pass safely through Strait of Hormuz</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://globalnation.inquirer.net/315412/iran-says-non-hostile-vessels-can-transit-strait-of-hormuz'>The Iranian foreign ministry states that vessels it classifies as non-hostile may pass through the Strait of Hormuz if they comply with its safety and security requirements, while excluding vessels linked to countries it accuses of involvement in the Iran war.</a> - inquirer.net</li></ul>